Can we replace the bucket info in the xml if we move to a new bucket (i.e., move from landing to SEFSC)? 
Gemini answer:
Yes. In standard ISO 19115/19139 documents, bucket names and folder prefixes are simply text values stored inside XML tags (such as gmd:transferOptions//gmd:onLine//gmd:linkage or aggregate identifier elements).
Because it is standard XML text, you can replace the old bucket name and parent path using either URI string replacement or parsed XML node updates.

